  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\n\nAt the beginning of next week, temperatures will begin to crawl back \ninto the 50s as the ridging pattern shifts eastward, funneling in \nwarm southerly air. By Wednesday, some spots will be reaching into \nthe 60s. This trend of warming will persist through at least the end \nof next week, keeping temperatures in the lower 60s past Wednesday.  \n\nThe next chance of precipitation (20-40%) will become a possibility \non Wednesday. The low level jet is forecasted to strengthen \novernight Tuesday into Wednesday morning, which will also funnel in \nmoisture, creating mixing in the lower levels. A cold front \nassociated with a surface low will also be on the move through the \nOAX CWA as well, adding in a lifting mechanism that could provide \naid in yielding showers for the area. Timing of this precipitation \nis still largely uncertain, and the models are beginning to show \nprecipitation taking a more southern track, which is why confidence \nin precipitation chances still remain from 20-40%.",
